# One byte sequence per file, on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites every text
# file's line endings on the way to disk. Two things in this repository read
# bytes rather than lines and cannot survive that: the API manifest reader
# parses the runtime's Rust source with anchored patterns, and the ingest test
# asserts a SHA-256 of compiled output against a committed digest. Both passed
# on Linux and macOS and failed on Windows for reasons that had nothing to do
# with either — see the first release dry run (#134).
#
# `eol=lf` is the whole fix: the working tree matches the object store
# everywhere, so a digest means the same thing on all six targets.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched: fixtures whose bytes are the fixture.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.node binary
*.tgz binary
*.wav binary
